 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Browser agent tools (WebMCP)
+
+The shared layout registers browser tools once per document, including across
+Astro client-side navigation. Browsers without WebMCP keep the normal UI. Both
+`document.modelContext` and the earlier `navigator.modelContext` are detected.
+No MCP server or additional credentials are required; requests use the existing
+same-origin article API and browser session.
+
+Always available in supporting browsers:
+
+| Tool | Parameters | Result |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `find_articles` | `query` (nonempty string) | Articles matching titles or summaries, with links |
+| `get_article` | `slug` | Article metadata, summary and link |
+| `get_reading_list` | None | Saved articles for the current session |
+| `set_article_saved` | `slug`, `saved` (boolean) | Desired saved state and updated list |
+
+The header forms expose `open_search` and `open_reading_list`. Once opened,
+the flyouts expose `search_articles` (`query`) and `remove_saved_article`
+(`slug`, selected from saved articles). These forms use `toolname`,
+`tooldescription`, named controls and `toolautosubmit`; agent submissions return
+structured results through `SubmitEvent.respondWith`. Ordinary form submissions
+use the same handlers and keep results visible. Saved-state changes also update
+mounted bookmark buttons and the reading-list flyout.
+
+The integration follows Chrome's [declarative WebMCP API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/declarative-api)
+and [imperative WebMCP API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api).
+
+Run the server-free checks with Node 22.18+:
+
+```sh
+pnpm test
+pnpm build
+```
